Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement. Question: Is the 'ability to consummate' concept, as outlined in the following clause, subject to Material Adverse Effect carveouts? Option A: No Option B: Yes

Merger Agreement Clause: "Consummation Condition" means that the Company’s ability to consummate the merger shall be considered impaired only if, in aggregate, one or more events cause either (i) a material delay beyond the agreed threshold or (ii) an impairment that is not solely attributable to general market fluctuations, judicial delays, or routine regulatory modifications. Specifically, any delay or impairment arising exclusively from macroeconomic volatility, standard adjustments in regulatory accounting policies, or normal variations in currency exchange and credit ratings shall be expressly excluded from being deemed a Material Adverse Effect. However, if such events impose a disproportionate and unique burden on the Company compared to its industry peers, the resulting impairment may be taken into account."
